 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Dire que",
     "texto": [
      "With **dire que** we use **que** and a clause: **Thomas a dit que Paul était fatigué** (Thomas said that Paul was tired).",
      "If the verb that introduces the report is in the past, the tense depends on when what was said happens: present → imparfait (simultaneous), passé composé → plus-que-parfait (earlier), future → conditionnel (later)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tenses that stay the same",
     "texto": [
      "The imparfait, the plus-que-parfait and the conditionnel usually stay the same: **Il a dit qu'il viendrait** (he said he would come).",
      "If the information is still valid, the present can also be kept; the sequence of tenses follows the meaning, not an automatic shift."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Watch out",
     "texto": [
      "If what is said is a general truth, the tense does not change: **Il a dit que la Terre est ronde** (he said the Earth is round)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Direct speech",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Indirect speech (past)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
